**Summary of extraction:**

The stem-system specification describes a **Clubhouse Manager** -- a Next.js 15 club member management system for STEM研究部 with Discord OAuth authentication via Supabase. I extracted **14 program graphs** covering all functional units:

- **Authentication flows** (SG-001 to SG-002): Discord OAuth callback with open-redirect prevention, session middleware
- **Built-in OAuth 2.0 provider** (SG-003 to SG-006): Authorization endpoint with PKCE S256, consent/code generation, token exchange with bcrypt client auth and JWT signing, userinfo endpoint
- **Member operations** (SG-007 to SG-009): Registration, profile update with admin/self permission branching, admin member management with logical deletion
- **Admin management** (SG-010 to SG-011): Team CRUD with member assignment and leader designation, generation-to-Discord-role mapping
- **Infrastructure** (SG-012 to SG-014): Discord bot sync (fire-and-forget), Supabase client creation (SSR vs admin with RLS implications), daily encrypted database backup pipeline

Key invariants captured include: PKCE S256 enforcement, open-redirect sanitization, RLS bypass via admin client, logical vs physical deletion semantics, fire-and-forget Discord bot calls, and AES-256 backup encryption.

